Hi Enrico,

We have some documentation related to this in our parallelization example <https://r-nimble.org/nimbleExamples/parallelizing_NIMBLE.html>, which you may have seen. Specifically toward the end of that example there is some discussion of user-defined distributions. Based on that, you'll need to assign `dAOR` and `rAOR` into the global environment on the workers. The slightly tricky thing in your case is that you are not explicitly defining `rAOR`. It is being defined automatically by NIMBLE in the `nimbleModel()` call.

So if you do the following it should work:
- insert this code after you define dAOR:
assign('dAOR', dAOR, envir = .GlobalEnv)
- insert this code just after the nimbleModel() call
assign('rAOR', rAOR, envir = .GlobalEnv)

(It's also fine to insert both additional lines of code just after the `nimbleModel()` call, but the key thing is only to do the second after `rAOR` is created behind the scenes.

-chris

