To follow up on Wei's point, if you have `calculate=FALSE` (which will prevent the warnings) you need to make sure that all of the nodes that are deterministic are set before you do the simulation (in particular po[2,1:2], px[2,1:2], alive[1,f[1]], alive[2,f[2],alive[3,f[3]], alive[4,f[4]], alive[5,f[5]]). Then the simulation should work fine and without warnings.

If you have `calculate=TRUE`, then you don't need to worry about manually setting those deterministic nodes yourself, but you will see the warnings, but they are just warnings and not a problem here.

You can work through this yourself by individually simulating the elements of sim_nodes in order one by one.

sim_model$simulate(sim_nodes[1])
sim_model$simulate(sim_nodes[2])
etc.

while looking at the values currently in the model nodes.

-chris

