> I think you need to turn on 'calculate = TRUE'  when building the model or run 'sim_model$calculate()' before you simulate data to make sure you can actually generate data by simulation. This is because otherwise all variables except for phi and p in the model do not have values assigned and then the simulated data are all NaN. After doing the calculations, although you still see the warning message, you will be able to generate data. The dynamic index message is actually a warning, not an error, due to the invalid index values ( in your case not currently available before you simulate). I would say this is not a big deal here, nothing to worry about. I do not see a neat way to handle this, but other people may have some good ideas.
